  "body": [
    "Kensington's difficulties compound one another. Poverty, homelessness, addiction, mental health, housing exploitation and systemic racism operate as a single problem rather than six. The studio began by mapping those relationships, then asked what one piece of architecture could reasonably address.",
    "The proposal is a core: one block carrying the six things the neighborhood lacks — jobs and education, equal opportunity, rehabilitation, reasonable housing, fair housing practice, and comprehensive support. The programs are interleaved rather than stacked in separate buildings, so reaching one makes the next easier to reach.",
    "On Jasper Street, under the elevated line, the block keeps its existing brick shells and threads new work between them. The Maker Factory holds exhibition space, hydroponic labs and workshops; the transit building becomes one long flexible room; a warehouse becomes the Foundations of Kensington Past museum; temporary residences sit above. At the center is the Core itself, a splash pad and stepped open ground under a canopy, free to enter and tied to no single program."
  ],
